  "findings": [
    {
      "status": "confirmed",
      "text": "The Giovanni data box is the single point -111.875, 33.5, the centre of POWER cell [247, 109]."
    },
    {
      "status": "confirmed",
      "text": "A fresh live read of POWER T2M_MAX gives the bundled yearly counts in 45 of 45 years."
    },
    {
      "status": "confirmed",
      "text": "Giovanni T2MMAX is higher than POWER T2M_MAX on every one of the 16,436 days (minimum +0.003 degC, mean +0.22 degC, steady by decade), so every count difference is a day that Giovanni puts at or above 43.3 degC and POWER puts below it."
    },
    {
      "status": "confirmed",
      "text": "Rounding Giovanni to the 2 decimals that POWER declares changes one day (2024: 46 to 47 days) and no engine statistic except OLS."
    },
    {
      "status": "confirmed",
      "text": "The POWER store defines T2M_MAX as the maximum hourly 2 m temperature (attribute 'definition', cell_methods 'time: max')."
    },
    {
      "status": "unverified",
      "text": "Cause of the one-sided offset: M2SDNXSLV T2MMAX is probably the maximum over the model time step, while POWER takes the maximum of hourly values; a maximum over finer sampling is never lower. Check the MERRA-2 File Specification (GMAO Office Note 9) for statD_2d_slv_Nx and the POWER methodology page."
    }
  ],
